---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research methodology"
  description="How church software entries are selected, sourced, verified, dated, corrected and separated from editorial assessment and commercial interests."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Methodology" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container page-grid">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Trust and evidence</p>
        <h1>Research methodology</h1>
        <p>
          The directory aims to make the status of every important claim visible.
          A supplier source can establish what the supplier publishes; it does not
          amount to hands-on testing or independent certification.
        </p>

        <h2>Which products are included</h2>
        <p>
          A product must have an active official site and plausible relevance to
          UK church administration, ministry or operations. The first engineering
          phase contains only fifty-one representative entries.
        </p>

        <h2>How facts are researched</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Prefer official product, pricing, support and policy pages.</li>
          <li>Record the source URL, checked date and fields it supports.</li>
          <li>Keep structured facts separate from directory assessment.</li>
          <li>Use “Not confirmed” when the evidence does not establish an answer.</li>
          <li>Do not infer compliance from general marketing language.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Verification statuses</h2>
        <dl class="stack">
          <div>
            <dt>Verified</dt>
            <dd>
              The important fields in scope have strong, current evidence and
              have received editorial review. None of the foundation listings
              currently uses this status.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Partially verified</dt>
            <dd>
              Several useful fields have current first-party sources, but
              material unknowns or unreviewed areas remain.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Needs review</dt>
            <dd>
              Evidence is old, incomplete or awaiting editorial review. Treat the
              entry as a lead for further research.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>

        <h2>Review cycle</h2>
        <p>
          The automated stale check currently flags entries more than 180 days
          after their last checked date. A recent date does not mean every product
          detail is complete.
        </p>

        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Users and suppliers may submit official evidence. Corrections are
          assessed on evidence, regardless of commercial status. The submission
          endpoint is not connected in this foundation build.
        </p>

        <h2>Commercial independence</h2>
        <p>
          Affiliate links are used only where a relationship is confirmed and
          disclosed beside the relevant link. They must not guarantee positive
          coverage or ranking. Any sponsored listing must be clearly labelled
          and is held to the same research and editorial standards.
        </p>
      </article>
      <aside class="aside-card">
        <h2>Important boundary</h2>
        <p>
          Churches should verify legal, security, safeguarding, tax, data-hosting
          and contractual matters directly with suppliers and appropriate
          advisers.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/update-a-listing/">Point to a correction</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
